From: vbardales <virginie.bardales@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:10:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(test): the language steps shared their text, and the
 scenario proves nothing yet

Running language-steps.feature, which I had not done before pushing it, found
two things.

The action and the assertion were both "the language is {string}". The step
table ignores the keyword, so every scenario failed with "Ambiguous step" in a
few milliseconds. The action is now "the language is set to {string}".

Past that, the scenario fails: switching to French took about 7 seconds, but
switching back to English never completed within 35, so the first scenario
times out and the second reads French. The log has no "No active language!"
line, so the run never entered the window this PR fixes - it survived because
nothing hit it, which is not evidence that the fix held. The comment I had
written, that the file never reaches its second scenario on the broken code,
was a claim I had not checked.

The feature is tagged @wip with the above written at its head, so it stays out
of default runs instead of sitting red on an open PR. It needs running against
the unfixed build, and the English timeout needs an explanation, before it
claims anything.

AI-assisted: Claude Code

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
